  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Standard Bearer" id="5093-098d-a6e2-9246" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Imperial Guard units with a model within 12&quot; of the Standard Bearer may re-roll any failed Morale checks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Medi-pack" id="16d3-73ab-2527-3e33" hidden="false">
      <description>Medi-packs allow a unit with a medic to ignore the first failed saving throw it rolls in every turn. The medi-pack may not be used on any model which suffers instant death or that has been hit by a close combat weapon that allows no Amrour save. It may not be used if the medic is in base contact with an enemy model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Comm-Link" id="fcaa-7305-6950-d142" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Command HQ or Command Section has a comm-link, then one squad with a comm-link each turn can use the Officer’s Leadership value no matter where they are on the battlefield (normally they’d have to be within 12&quot;). You can use the comm-link anytime, such as right before a Leadership test or even if the command unit is still in reserve.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master-crafted Weapons" id="bfa6-639a-4ff4-e20e" hidden="false">
      <description>The bearer may re-roll one failed to hit roll per turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Trademark Item" id="0630-f0bd-6da5-e593" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit led by a person who carries a trademark item may re-roll any failed Morale or Pinning checks it suffers. However, if the character is slain, the unit must pass a Morale test to avoid falling back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Scanner" id="c061-bcf5-ed69-d507" hidden="false">
      <description>If enemy infiltrators set up with 4D6&quot; of a model with a surveyor then the model is allowed to take a &apos;free&apos; shot at them. If the model is part of a unit, the whole unit may shoot. These shots are taken before the battle begins and may cause the infiltrators to fall back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Immobile" id="468c-bd45-5505-589a" hidden="false">
      <description>Once deployed, the model may not be moved unless towed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Amphibious" id="f779-54b0-691f-402d" hidden="false">
      <description>Treat all water features as clear terrain when moving</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Anti-Air" id="3113-8762-7d4c-7334" hidden="false">
      <description>Roll to hit aircraft using the firers normal BS</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Smoke Launchers" id="8573-0653-d612-e4de" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per game, after completing movement, a vehicle with smoke launchers may trigger them. The vehicle cannot fire and use its smoke launchers in the same turn. Any penetrating hits scored by the enemy in the next Shooting phase count as glancing hits.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Searchlight" id="4877-41b8-d9e1-6da3" hidden="false">
      <description>During Night Fighting missions, one enemy unit spotted by the vehicle can be fired at by any other Imperial Guard units in range and with line of fire. However, the vehicle using the Searchlight will then be exposed and can be fired at by any enemy units that are in range and line of sight of it until the next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Leadership" id="11ff-f612-addd-577e" hidden="false"/>
    <rule name="Rough Terrain Modification" id="7023-343a-0f96-bd4e" hidden="false">
      <description>A vehicle that moves no more than 6&quot; may re-rolled failed Difficult Terrain tests</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Camo Cloak" id="647d-f731-5d52-f8e4" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Tanith squad adds +1 to any cover saves they are allowed. In addition, opponents roll 2D6x2 instead of 2D6x3 when attempting to spot Tanith troops in a Night Fight.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Tanith Knife" id="36d3-c20f-b78f-7bf9" hidden="false">
      <description>A unit led by a person who carries a trademark item may re-roll any failed Morale or Pinning checks it suffers. However, if the character is slain, the unit must pass a Morale test to avoid falling back.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Absolute Direction" id="ea86-cee4-a47b-c214" hidden="false">
      <description>All Tanith units may re-roll failed Reserve rolls. If a Tanith unit is affected by a result on the Alaitoc Ranger Disruption table from Codex: Craftworld Eldar, roll a dice, the result is ignored on the roll of a 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Holy Relic" id="bcc1-8c37-a9c9-b60b" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per battle. On any turn the model with the relic does not move they may reveal it. All friendly models that are within 2D6&quot; gain +1 Attacks for the rest of that turn. The relic may be revealed in the opposing player&apos;s turn assuming the model with the relic did not move in the previous turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bionics" id="1973-df4c-dfdf-8af6" hidden="false">
      <description>When a model with bionics is killed, instead place it on its side. Roll a D6 at the start of the next turn: on a roll of 6 the model stands back up with 1 wound, but on any other roll it is removed as a casualty.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Carapace Armor" id="f1bf-49f9-4094-c2f9" hidden="false">
      <description>4+ Armour Save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Refractor Field" id="b3db-ab15-ba69-979f" hidden="false">
      <description>Gain a 5+ invulnerable save</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Targeter" id="1c37-d83d-2234-7c18" hidden="false">
      <description>Models equipped with a targeter are allowed to pre-measure the range to a target before they decide who to shoot at in the Shooting phase. This ability must be used after all Guess ranged weapons have been used this turn, otherwise those weapons cannot fire this turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Iron Discipline" id="23bf-b1d4-efd9-39e9" hidden="false">
      <description>Any unit using the Leadership ability of a Cadian Officer with the Iron Discipline ability for Morale or Pinning test ignores the -1 modifier for being under half strength and may regroup even if below half strength.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sharpshooters" id="0a5e-9493-a5b1-e5d5" hidden="false">
      <description>Any Cadian infantry model with a BS of 3 may make a single re-roll of a shooting to hit roll of 1. This has no effect when firing plasma weapons or sniper rifles.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
